# sites-cf281a941.kzs -- logical sites of case C1 for the instrumented family (kzs-sites 2, kairos/docs/event_semantics.md
# section 3), CF 281a941 (pre-fix) + BP b051eb0 on either cFS bundle candidate (plan/C1_build_manifest.md section 1).
# Stage D: every site of the F0 plan observe/sites-cf281a941.kzp (33) has a counterpart here with the same label, and
# an `equiv ... backends=f0,gcc-plugin status=unconfirmed` line that names the F0 site and how the two positions relate
# (IR section 9.3: a common name is not an equivalence; it is confirmed only with evidence, stage E).  The GCC-only
# sites (no F0 counterpart, no equiv line) are marked "GCC only".
#
# Positions follow the profile's linearization points (20_ops.kzp `lp at`) at the source statement: a call(X) point is
# the call of X (at-call where the profile reads the call's arguments, after-call where it reads the result), a
# store(T.f) point is the store statement, a memset(T) point is that memset call.  F0 had to approximate some of them in
# the Release binaries (no line table, inline memsets, tail jumps); the equiv refs say where.  Values are the operands
# the original code uses (arguments, results, stored values, the enclosing function's parameter values) and an out
# parameter read by the same thread right after a call (from=out<k>, event_semantics.md 8.1).  A string is copied only
# where the original code validated the pointer before the point (string=validated with the citation).  The F0 slot
# `return_address` (the word at the top of the stack, used by F0 to pair an entry with its return and to place a
# request's calling code) has no counterpart: entry and return are paired by `link`; the calling function of a request
# made at a function-entry binding is not determined (docs/schema.md section 12.3.1).
#
# Line numbers are those of the files at the revisions below.  The cited OSAL, cFE and PSP files are byte-identical in
# the two bundle candidates (cmp, 2026-10-26): module 1 (core of 1df262a) and module 4 (core of 1b0b338) have the same
# sites; the build chooses the module (kzgcc default-module=), so binding ids of the two bundles differ.
# Stage F (cooperative gate, docs/event_semantics.md section 11): a control line at every site the C1 hold plans gate
# or release at (the gates 34, 44; the releases 35, 45 and 37, the GCC-only call of CFE_ES_ExitApp in CF), so that
# kz_rt_ctl is called there right after the observation hook; kz rtplan maps the plans' F0 labels onto them.
# Nothing here is a research condition.
kzs-sites 2
source cfs-bundle-1df262a rev=1df262a64a09f128357482d8f2e06b0fdfe84d37 ref="plan/C1_build_manifest.md section 1 (candidate A); cfe 6cccb3f5, osal f34759d6, psp bd4a2ea2"
source cfs-bundle-1b0b338 rev=1b0b338fd14030038fe1aa0e873c485bf5c851e2 ref="plan/C1_build_manifest.md section 1 (candidate B); cfe fef4a0da, osal b44f4ce7, psp bd4a2ea2"
source cf rev=281a94188cd7d885a5aed01ee041f3ece2b0486f ref="nasa/CF main of the manual workflow (plan/C1_build_manifest.md section 1)"
source bp rev=b051eb0d12bfe76c0230215c2ff851cfaa553ce4 ref="plan/C1_build_manifest.md section 1"
module 1 name=core-1df262a source=cfs-bundle-1df262a
module 4 name=core-1b0b338 source=cfs-bundle-1b0b338
module 2 name=cf.so source=cf
module 3 name=bp.so source=bp

